    rdfs:label "Evidence for Whale Fins used in Hat-Making, Brushes, Upholstery & Turnery: Simmonds (1892), Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products, scan p. 326"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "They are extensively used, when split, for caulking chairs, and for making rough brooms, and, when dyed black as a substitute for whalebone for umbrella ribs, and for stiffening bonnets."@en ;
